WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.405 --> 00:00:16.106
was the middle of July, and the hottest day ever.

2
00:00:17.127 --> 00:00:18.868
At least that's how it felt in my room.

3
00:00:20.708 --> 00:00:24.430
My skylight window was open, but it didn't help one bit.

4
00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:29.352
My fan was blowing, but it just seemed to blow more hot air around.

5
00:00:32.288 --> 00:00:35.749
I was even wearing my bathing suit, and I was still hot!

6
00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:39.771
My friends call me "Iggy the Incredible Inventor."

7
00:00:40.772 --> 00:00:43.513
But there was no way I could invent anything today.

8
00:00:45.073 --> 00:00:47.134
It was too hot for me to even think!

9
00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:51.276
Suddenly my fan stopped working.

10
00:00:55.938 --> 00:00:56.438
I called.

11
00:00:56.458 --> 00:00:58.359
"It's really hot in here!

12
00:00:58.879 --> 00:01:00.980
Can we get an air conditioner for my room?"

13
00:01:03.156 --> 00:01:05.158
My mom was getting ready to go shopping.

14
00:01:05.178 --> 00:01:11.062
"We can't fit an air conditioner in your tiny room, Iggy," she called from the kitchen.

15
00:01:11.082 --> 00:01:16.205
"Besides, I think the power just went out in the whole building.

16
00:01:17.366 --> 00:01:21.049
The lights aren't working and the air conditioner in the living room turned off."

17
00:01:21.509 --> 00:01:23.911
"My fan isn't working either!"

18
00:01:23.991 --> 00:01:24.531
I told her.

19
00:01:28.974 --> 00:01:31.116
My brother, Tate, stuck his head in my room.

20
00:01:32.232 --> 00:01:34.913
"Why don't you stop yelling and invent something?"

21
00:01:35.373 --> 00:01:35.934
he said.

22
00:01:35.954 --> 00:01:39.035
"I can't," I said.

23
00:01:39.055 --> 00:01:42.196
"It's so hot in here, my brain won't work."

24
00:01:43.457 --> 00:01:45.498
"Ha-ha!" Tate laughed.

25
00:01:46.178 --> 00:01:47.838
"Iggy's brain is melting!"

26
00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:52.480
not funny!"

27
00:01:52.961 --> 00:01:54.681
I cried, "Mom!

28
00:01:55.041 --> 00:01:56.862
Tate said my brain is melting!"

29
00:01:56.882 --> 00:02:02.433
"I want you two boys to get along while I'm gone," my mother said.

30
00:02:02.453 --> 00:02:05.534
"It's too hot to argue."

31
00:02:10.477 --> 00:02:13.839
A few minutes after my mom left, Molly knocked on our door.

32
00:02:16.681 --> 00:02:18.702
Her little brother, Caswell, was with her.

33
00:02:18.722 --> 00:02:24.885
"Wow," said Molly, sinking down on a chair in our living room.

34
00:02:24.905 --> 00:02:29.008
"It's even hotter in your apartment than it is in ours!

35
00:02:29.732 --> 00:02:32.114
Our power stopped working a few minutes ago."

36
00:02:32.134 --> 00:02:38.820
"The whole building is out of electricity," explained Tate.

37
00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:43.284
"Can you invent something to cool us off, Iggy?"

38
00:02:43.904 --> 00:02:44.665
asked Molly.

39
00:02:45.906 --> 00:02:46.727
I shook my head.

40
00:02:46.747 --> 00:02:50.410
"Nope." Caswell was looking at me.

41
00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:54.233
"Why do you have your bathing suit on, Iggy?"

42
00:02:54.673 --> 00:02:55.254
he asked.

43
00:02:55.274 --> 00:02:57.516
"Are you going swimming?"

44
00:02:59.476 --> 00:03:01.917
"I was trying to stay cool," I told him.

45
00:03:03.698 --> 00:03:05.939
Just then someone knocked on the door again.

46
00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:10.460
It was Josh and Jenny, from the floor below us.

47
00:03:11.621 --> 00:03:13.682
Josh's dog, Bunch, was with them.

48
00:03:14.782 --> 00:03:17.303
Poor Bunch was hanging his head and panting.

49
00:03:18.384 --> 00:03:19.624
He looked very hot.

50
00:03:23.326 --> 00:03:25.346
I brought him a bowl of water to drink.

51
00:03:25.366 --> 00:03:27.967
"Guess what?"

52
00:03:28.368 --> 00:03:31.670
said Jenny, while Bunch lapped noisily from the bowl.

53
00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:35.532
"Our air conditioner blew a fuse."

54
00:03:36.873 --> 00:03:38.314
"What's a fuse?"

55
00:03:38.855 --> 00:03:39.835
asked Caswell.

56
00:03:40.856 --> 00:03:41.637
Josh shrugged.

57
00:03:42.477 --> 00:03:43.918
"I'm not exactly sure.

58
00:03:44.438 --> 00:03:44.859
But Mr.

59
00:03:44.879 --> 00:03:48.141
Calabria said it made all the electricity in the building go out."

60
00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:53.084
"Just like Iggy's brain," said Tate.

61
00:03:53.104 --> 00:03:55.966
"It blew a fuse today too!"

62
00:03:55.986 --> 00:04:00.049
"Very funny," I said, frowning at him.

63
00:04:00.069 --> 00:04:04.630
"Iggy, can you think of a way to stay cool?"

64
00:04:05.151 --> 00:04:06.011
asked Jenny.

65
00:04:07.171 --> 00:04:09.332
I was sick of answering this question.

66
00:04:11.673 --> 00:04:14.034
Luckily, Molly answered for me this time.

67
00:04:14.054 --> 00:04:17.416
"Iggy can't think," she said.

68
00:04:17.436 --> 00:04:19.436
"He's too hot."

69
00:04:19.456 --> 00:04:23.858
"Wait a minute," I said.

70
00:04:23.878 --> 00:04:26.079
"I do have an idea!"

71
00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:28.380
"I hope it's a good one!"

72
00:04:28.856 --> 00:04:29.557
said Josh.

73
00:04:29.577 --> 00:04:32.960
"If I get any hotter, I'll blow a fuse too."

74
00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:39.185
"Well, it's not a great idea," I said, grinning.

75
00:04:39.205 --> 00:04:42.848
"But it could lead to a great idea!"

76
00:04:42.868 --> 00:04:44.770
"What is it?"

77
00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:45.830
asked Molly.

78
00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:50.174
"I'm going to put an ice pack on my head," I said.

79
00:04:50.194 --> 00:04:52.556
"That will cool off my brain.

80
00:04:52.916 --> 00:04:56.199
Then I'll be able to think of my next incredible invention!"
